.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt ZFS-KEYSLOT 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zfs-keyslot
.Nd add, change, remove, or list the key slots of an encrypted dataset
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm add
.Op Fl S Ar slot
.Op Fl o Ar keyformat Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl o Ar pbkdf2iters Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm set
.Fl S Ar slot
.Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm remove
.Fl S Ar slot
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm list
.Op Fl Hjp
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An encrypted dataset is encrypted with a master key, and that master key is
stored wrapped by the wrapping key of its encryption root.
The wrapping key is derived from the key the user supplies, so a key slot holds
one wrapping of the encryption root's wrapping key.
Any slot can unlock the same dataset, while each slot has its own key material,
key format, and source, which allows one dataset to be unlocked with several
independent keys.
.Pp
Slot 1 is the primary slot.
It always exists, is created by
.Nm zfs Cm create ,
and is the wrapping that
.Nm zfs Cm change-key
replaces.
.Nm zfs Cm load-key
reads slot 1 unless
.Fl S
selects another slot.
Slots 2 and above are added with
.Nm zfs Cm keyslot
and require the
.Sy keyslots
pool feature
.Pq see Xr zpool-features 7 .
Adding a slot does not change the dataset's keys or re-encrypt any data; it adds
another wrapping of the same wrapping key.
.Pp
Slots belong to the encryption root, so every verb takes the encryption root as
its target; naming a dataset below it is refused with a message naming the root.
Every verb also fails on a dataset that is not encrypted.
Adding or removing a slot requires the root's key to be loaded, so
.Sy keystatus
must be
.Sy available .
Changing a slot's source and listing slots read only metadata and work on a
locked root.
.Bl -tag -width ""
.It Xo
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm add
.Op Fl S Ar slot
.Op Fl o Ar keyformat Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl o Ar pbkdf2iters Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Xc
Adds a key slot to the encryption root, wrapping its wrapping key under the new
slot's key.
The key is read or prompted for exactly as
.Nm zfs Cm create
does for a new dataset, and the slot's key format, salt, and iteration count are
recorded with the slot.
The number of the new slot is printed.
Slot 1 is the primary slot and cannot be created; when
.Fl S
is omitted, the lowest free slot is allocated.
.Bl -tag -width "-S"
.It Fl S Ar slot
Use the given slot number instead of allocating the lowest free one.
The value must be 2 or greater and the slot must be free.
.It Fl o Ar keyformat Ns = Ns Ar value
The format of the new slot's key: one of
.Sy raw ,
.Sy hex ,
or
.Sy passphrase .
This property is required; see
.Xr zfsprops 7 .
.It Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
The source used when this slot is loaded.
The default is
.Sy prompt .
A value of
.Sy none
is refused for encrypted datasets.
The location is stored in the
.Sy keylocation_ Ns Ar slot
property.
.It Fl o Ar pbkdf2iters Ns = Ns Ar value
The number of PBKDF2 iterations used to derive a
.Sy passphrase
slot's key; see
.Xr zfsprops 7 .
.El
.Pp
The command fails if the
.Sy keyslots
feature is not enabled, if the key is not loaded, or if the requested slot is
already in use.
.It Xo
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm set
.Fl S Ar slot
.Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Xc
Changes the stored source of an existing slot in place.
Nothing is re-wrapped: the slot keeps its key material, and only the location it
is loaded from changes.
Slot 1 edits the
.Sy keylocation
property; any other slot edits
.Sy keylocation_ Ns Ar slot .
The slot must exist.
.Bl -tag -width "-S"
.It Fl S Ar slot
The slot to edit.
This option is required.
.It Fl o Ar keylocation Ns = Ns Ar value
The new source.
This option is required and is the only property accepted, because a slot's key
format and iteration count are fixed when the slot is created.
.El
.Pp
The edit is authorized by the
.Sy keylocation
permission, not by
.Sy keyslot .
.It Xo
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm remove
.Fl S Ar slot
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Xc
Removes a key slot.
The slot's key material and the location stored for it are deleted in the same
transaction, so the slot can no longer unlock the dataset.
A location that the dataset received from a stream is deleted as well, so no
stored source is left behind for a slot that does not exist.
Slot 1 cannot be removed, and slot 0 is not a slot.
The key must be loaded, so a recovery slot cannot be removed while the root is
locked.
.Pp
Removal is not secure erasure: like
.Nm zfs Cm change-key ,
it does not overwrite the previous wrapping on disk, so that wrapping may remain
recoverable by forensic analysis.
See the warning in
.Xr zfs-load-key 8
for what to do when a key is compromised.
.It Xo
.Nm zfs
.Cm keyslot
.Cm list
.Op Fl Hjp
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar volume
.Xc
Prints one row per slot, slot 1 included, sorted by slot number: the slot
number, key format, PBKDF2 salt, PBKDF2 iteration count, and the stored
location.
A slot with no stored location is shown with a dash.
Only metadata is read, so the command works on a locked root and never prints
key material.
.Bl -tag -width "-H"
.It Fl H
Do not print a header line.
.It Fl j
Print the rows as JSON, as a
.Sy keyslots
object keyed by slot number.
.It Fl p
Print numeric values; the key format is then printed as the numeric value of the
.Sy keyformat
property.
.El
.El
.Ss Delegation
.Nm zfs Cm keyslot Cm add
and
.Nm zfs Cm keyslot Cm remove
require the
.Sy keyslot
permission, which must be granted on the encryption root.
.Nm zfs Cm keyslot Cm set
requires the
.Sy keylocation
permission, and
.Nm zfs Cm keyslot Cm list
is not gated, because it prints only metadata that is already readable through
.Xr zfsprops 7 .
See
.Xr zfs-allow 8 .
.Pp
A user granted
.Sy keyslot
can add a slot using key material of their own choosing while the root is
unlocked, and revoking the permission does not remove that slot; it has to be
listed, and removed, explicitly.
Grant
.Sy keyslot
with the same care as
.Sy load-key .
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zfsprops 7 ,
.Xr zpool-features 7 ,
.Xr zfs-allow 8 ,
.Xr zfs-create 8 ,
.Xr zfs-load-key 8
